$ bash authoring/apple-studio/pipeline/generate_catalog.sh
Wrote .../framework-catalog.md: 400 entries

First result (before any post-processing):
  1 file changed, 391 insertions(+), 391 deletions(-)
That diff is noise. generate_catalog.sh emits bare /documentation/ URLs. The
committed catalog instead carried a trailing ".md" on 390 of its 400 entries (the
Phase 8 rewrite, 2026-09-13). The generator was never taught that rewrite. With the
bare URLs, tests/apple-doc-links.test.ts failed ("every page-form Apple documentation
link in apple-studio ends in .md").

Fix applied to the generated file, not to the generator: re-append ".md" to every
/documentation/ URL except the nine legacy roots the test pins as exceptions
(applicationservices, coreservices, installer_js, iokit, kernel, playgroundbluetooth,
playgroundsupport, tvmljs, webkitjs). The HIG entry is not a /documentation/ URL and
is left alone. "rewrote 390" matches the 390 the old file carried.

$ git diff --stat   (after the re-append)
 .../apple-frameworks/references/framework-catalog.md | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

Entry count: 400 before, 400 after. One line is the "> generated:" date
(2026-09-02 -> 2026-10-18). The other six are reworded abstracts. No framework was
added or removed.

## added entry lines (6)
+ - **Advanced Commerce API** — Support Apple In-App Purchases through the App Store for exceptionally large catalogs of custom one-time purchases, subscriptions, and subscriptions with optional add-ons. — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/advancedcommerceapi.md
+ - **App Tracking Transparency** — Request authorization to access app-related data that your app can use to track the person or the device. — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/apptrackingtransparency.md
+ - **Apple Ads** — Drive app discovery by creating and managing campaigns with the Apple Ads Campaign Management API. — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/apple_ads.md
+ - **AVKit** — Adopt the system’s video playback interfaces, and integrate your camera app with capture hardware. — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/avkit.md
+ - **StoreKit Test** — Create and automate tests in Xcode for your app’s subscription and Apple In-App Purchase transactions, and SKAdNetwork implementations. — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/storekittest.md
+ - **StoreKit** — Support Apple In-App Purchases and interactions with the App Store. — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/storekit.md

